      "math_academy_id": "e-6711",
      "problem": "What is the coefficient of $a^2b$ in the product $(a+b)(a^2 + ab + b^2)?$",
      "worked_solution": "We distribute both terms of the binomial in the first set of parentheses to the trinomial in the second set of parentheses. Then, we simplify.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(a+b)({a}^{2}+ab+{b}^{2}) & = \\\\ a({a}^{2}+ab+{b}^{2})+b({a}^{2}+ab+{b}^{2}) & = \\\\ {a}^{3}+{a}^{2}b+a{b}^{2}+{a}^{2}b+a{b}^{2}+{b}^{3} & = \\\\ {a}^{3}+2{a}^{2}b+2a{b}^{2}+{b}^{3} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of $a^2 b$ is $2.$",
